## K-uniform extension

The reduction has exposed a uniform recurrence, but not yet a uniform kill.
For `b=K-2`, `r=K-6`, the quotient recurrence `REC_n` is closed in K. For
`7<=K<=13` (in particular K=10,11), the other terms in `E-lambda*f` are below
degree `K+6`, so the terminal target is

```text
Theta_K = y^K*(y-x)^2*sum_(i=0..4) e_i*x^(4-i)*y^i,
e_0=1/(5K-6),
e_i=((5-i)K/((5-i)K-6))*e_(i-1).
```

At K=10 the initial divisibility exponent changes. In general write
`psi=y^s*phi`, `s=ceil((K-5)/2)`, so `s=3` for K=10,11. An exact symbolic-Q
expansion of `REC_3`, independently checked twice, gives after `phi=y*v`

```text
K=10: y | p_2*v,
K=11: y^2 | v*W,  W=(y-x)*v^2-18*v*tau-12*mu*p_2.
```

Thus K=10 has the two exhaustive closed charts `v=y*w` and `p_2=y*zeta`.
K=11 has the three valuation charts

```text
ord_y(v)>=2;
ord_y(v)>=1 and ord_y(W)>=1;
ord_y(W)>=2.
```

Overlaps are retained; no factor is localized. The same audit recovers

```text
