+## 5. Q4 - Finish And Scope
+
+**Answer.** The fixed-degree skeleton strategy generalizes as a finite method,
+not as an all-degree proof. It can prove "no pair of this degree" when the
+census is finite and every skeleton is killed. It does not by itself prove the
+two-point stratum for all degrees, because the screened census is cofinally
+nonempty and the current routing interface is unproved.
+
+The coordinator framing should stay corrected in three ways.
+
+```text
+1. Degree-wide (99,66) is not plane JC2.
+   It is the published small-degree hole after a finite N1 list is killed.
+
+2. H1 + H2 along Moh's two-point M_s=n-2 line is not the whole plane
+   Jacobian conjecture.
+   One-place/Abhyankar-Moh, U-negative, s'>2 arrivals, and route-to-state
+   remain outside the proved interface.
+
+3. "Enumerate skeletons at a degree, kill each" is a semidecision procedure.
+   It becomes an all-degree proof only after a uniform theorem bounds or
+   eliminates the infinite family of skeletons.  The 20260903 cofinal K16
+   family is the direct warning sign.
+```
+
+Typed bounded claims:
+
+```text
+For a fixed degree D:
+  if a source-gated census gives finitely many admissible skeletons and every
+  split/no-split chart for each skeleton has an exact unit certificate, then
+  that degree is closed in the declared two-point scope.
+
+For all D:
+  current evidence gives no finite all-D kill list.  The bounded object is not
+  "all skeletons"; it is a theorem parameter, for example K16's t or a row
+  invariant controlling the augmented Schur residue.
+
+For the two-point stratum:
+  K16 + all fixed-degree kills + routing maps would still need H1 all-degree
+  minor-empty or a replacement theorem.  The D<=200 H1 census is not an
+  all-degree theorem.
+```
+
+Cheapest test:
+
+```text
+After batch3 final_status, run a theorem-interface composition pass:
+  input the exact N1 kill certificates, K16 EN-norm target, H1 pilot rows,
+  and routing-map obligations;
+  output which hypotheses feed which conclusions and which scope gaps remain.
+Wall: <2 hours, no CAS beyond manifest/hash reads and tiny source checks.
+```
+
+The single most valuable next mathematical object is the K16 EN-norm
+`N_t=Norm(widehat Q_t)`. The N1 finite kill list is the highest-value near-term
+deliverable, but it is already running. If batch3 fails, S1 becomes the
